course: dictionary
lesson: 6427
title: Mycelium: the hidden body of a fungus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists often find that the part you can see is not the whole thing. «A mushroom is only the fruiting part of a fungus; the main body is mycelium.» The word after the semicolon tells you what the main body is, so mycelium must be the large hidden part, and the mushroom is just the top.
explain: «The real fungus is a hidden web of threads, the mycelium, spread through the soil or a log like a giant tangle of white cotton.» The clues are hidden, soil, log, tangle and white cotton. Try your meaning in the sentence: the real fungus is a hidden mass of white threads. It still makes sense, so you have worked it out from the context.
explain: Mycelium is a noun, and it has a special plural, mycelia. «A fairy ring forms where the threads grow outwards in a circle» shows that the threads spread out from one place, so mycelium is not a single thing but a whole network.
fact: Mycelium is a mass of thin white threads that belong to a fungus.
fact: Mycelium grows underground or inside rotting wood.
fact: Mushrooms grow out of mycelium, so a mushroom is only the fruiting part of the fungus.
fact: The plural of mycelium is mycelia.
fact: Mycelium is sometimes called the «wood wide web», because it links tree roots and helps plants share food.
exercise: «The mushroom you see is only the fruit; the real fungus is a hidden web of threads.» What is the mycelium? | A type of tree root | The mushroom sitting on top of the soil | A kind of rotten log | *The hidden threads of a fungus
exercise: «...spread through the soil or a log like a giant tangle of white cotton.» Where can mycelium grow? | Only on the tops of mushrooms | On the middle of a busy road | In the sky above the clouds | *Underground or inside rotting wood
exercise: What is the plural of mycelium? | *mycelia | mycelies | myceliums | mycels
test: «The mycelium spreads through the soil like a giant tangle of white cotton.» What does mycelium look like? | *Thin white threads | Large green leaves | Long brown roots | Hard grey stones
test: Some people call mycelium the «wood wide web». Why? | *It links tree roots and helps plants share food | It only grows on the top of the soil | It is a web spun by spiders in the forest | It is a type of mushroom you can eat
exam: Ella says mycelium is the mushroom you pick for dinner. Which statement is correct? | Mycelium is a tree root that grows above the ground | Mycelium is the mushroom you pick | Mycelium is a kind of rotten log | *Mycelium is the hidden web of threads, and the mushroom is only the fruiting part
